# The GStreamer plugins linked into the Android build, one per line.
#
# Read by `build-aux/android/gstreamer-static-plugins.sh`, which turns this list
# into both the C registration and the link line, so the two cannot drift apart.
# Names are plugin names, not element names: the archive for `foo` is
# `lib/gstreamer-1.0/libgstfoo.a`.
#
# Every entry costs binary size, so this is a list of things something actually
# asks for rather than everything that might one day be useful. On a dynamic
# build GStreamer would discover plugins by scanning a directory; here nothing
# is discovered, and an element that is not reachable from this list fails at
# `gst_element_factory_make` with "no such element".

# --- the machinery, needed by any pipeline at all ---
coreelements        # filesrc, fakesink, queue, capsfilter, typefind
typefindfunctions   # the content sniffing decodebin dispatches on
playback            # uridecodebin3, decodebin3, urisourcebin
gio                 # giosrc, for the URIs GFile hands out that are not file://

# --- audio conversion and measurement ---
audioconvert
audioresample
audioparsers        # framing for elementary streams that arrive without it
level               # the meter the voice-message waveform is built from
app                 # appsink; the video thumbnailer will want it

# --- containers ---
ogg
matroska            # .mkv and .webm
isomp4              # .mp4 and .m4a

# --- audio decoders ---
opus                # what Matrix voice messages actually are
vorbis
flac
wavparse
mpg123              # mp3
id3demux            # an mp3 with an ID3 tag is `application/x-id3` until this
                    # strips it, and then nothing downstream is reachable.
                    # Measured: without it, a tagged mp3 gives no duration and
                    # no waveform, while ogg, wav and flac are unaffected.

# --- video, and everything else `libav` decodes ---
videoconvertscale   # videoconvert, for the thumbnailer and the video sink
videoparsersbad     # h264parse and friends, which decodebin3 inserts ahead of
                    # a decoder for a stream that arrives out of a container
libav               # the decoders themselves, in software. `androidmedia` is
                    # the hardware alternative and is not usable yet; see below

# --- playback ---
volume              # playbin's own volume element, which it makes by name
autodetect          # autoaudiosink, which is what playbin picks when nothing
                    # else is set
opensles            # and what autoaudiosink then finds. OpenSL ES is an NDK
                    # API, so unlike MediaCodec it needs nothing from Java

# Deliberately absent, and why:
#
#   * `androidmedia`, the hardware codecs, reached through MediaCodec. It wants
#     `gst_android_get_application_class_loader`, which GStreamer core defines
#     in `gstandroid.c.o` — and that object also defines `JNI_OnLoad`, which
#     GTK already defines in `gdkandroidruntime.c`. Referencing the one drags in
#     the other and the link fails on a duplicate symbol. Nothing pulls that
#     object in today, which is why static GStreamer links at all.
#
#     There is a way through: an archive member is only extracted to satisfy an
#     *undefined* symbol, so defining `gst_android_get_application_class_loader`
#     ourselves leaves `gstandroid.c.o` unreferenced and the collision never
#     happens. GTK is handed the application classloader in
#     `gdk_android_initialize`, which is exactly what that function has to
#     return. Untried; `libav` decodes the same formats in software today.
#   * `openh264` and `vpx`, which `libav` already covers.
#   * The camera and microphone sources (`ahc`, `ahs`). Both are in
#     `androidmedia`, and both are Java callbacks rather than an NDK API, so
#     they need more than the classloader above.
